@page "/how-to-play"
@inject NavigationManager Navigation

<div class="container mt-5">
    <div class="card shadow p-4 mx-auto" style="max-width: 900px;">
        <h1 class="text-center mb-4">How to Play</h1>

        <h3>Normal Mode</h3>
        <p>
            Guess the word in six tries or less. Each guess must be a valid
            5-letter word. Hit <strong>Enter</strong> to submit your guess!
        </p>

        <p>
            After each guess, the color of the tiles will change to show how
            close your guess was to the actual word.
        </p>

        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Yellow</strong> means that the letter is in the word,
                but in the wrong spot.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Green</strong> means that the letter is in the right
                spot and in the word.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Gray</strong> means the letter is not in the word at all.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <hr />

        <h3>All Yellows</h3>
        <p>
            Similar to Normal Mode, except every
            letter you guess that is in the word will appear yellow, even if it
            is already in the correct spot.
        </p>

        <hr />

        <h3>Only Greens</h3>
        <p>
            Similar to Normal Mode, except only letters that are in the word
            <em>and</em> in the correct spot are revealed.
        </p>

        <p>
            Any other letter (including letters that are in the word but in the
            wrong spot—letters that would normally be yellow) will appear gray.
        </p>

        <hr />

        <h3>Hard Mode</h3>
        <p>
            Once a letter has been colored yellow, it must appear in all
            subsequent guesses.
        </p>

        <p>
            Once a letter has been colored green, it must remain in that exact
            position in all subsequent guesses.
        </p>

        <hr />

        <h3>Vs. AI</h3>
        <p>
            Normal Mode, except once you've run out of guesses or correctly
            guessed the word, the AI's guesses will appear next to yours.
        </p>

        <p>
            The AI cannot see your guesses. Are you able to beat the AI?
        </p>

        <div class="text-center mt-4">
        <button class="btn btn-secondary" @onclick="GoHome">
            Back to Home
        </button>
        </div>

        @code {
            private void GoHome()
            {
                Navigation.NavigateTo("/");
            }
        }
    </div>
</div>